            <ArticleTitle>Osteoarthritis 1: Physiology, risk factors and causes of pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteoarthritis (OA) is a synovial joint disorder characterised by pain, stiffness, and restricted function. It is often classed as a degenerative disease because the affected joints deteriorate over time. This article, the first in a three-part series, describes the complex pathophysiology and causes of pain in OA, risk factors, and how it is diagnosed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
